/ fade in
(A signal...?)
> Who's texting me at 4 AM?
/ open phone
/ conversation: cipher casey
casey: hey uh
casey: i couldn't sleep
cipher: What's up?
casey: oh crap
casey: sorry if i woke you up
cipher: Don't worry about it.
casey: i had a hunch when that girl mentioned that there was something in the school basement
(She sends you a map of Northold, with a few dozen red points concentrating near the school.)
cipher: What's this?
casey: it's a map of the people who've been disappearing lately
> Right, I read about that, but...
cipher: That seems like way too many?
casey: i thought so too
casey: i don't know why but most of them didn't even make the news, there's way more than the public knew about
casey: i had to do some osint sleuthing to cross-reference missing persons reports, truancy, employment records...
casey: to be honest that part was a lot of fun
casey: but still scary
cipher: Yeah...
casey: they're getting faster.
cipher: Hm?
casey: there were months between the first disappearances i found, now there's at least one every day
casey: but no one is saying anything
cipher: And you think it has something to do with the monsters we fought and the thing under the school?
casey: i found people posting about it online, but their accounts got deleted the next day
casey: they were talking about the same things we saw
cipher: Do you mind if I invite Mauve?
cipher: She's the girl we spoke with on Monday.
cipher: I think she'll have some valuable insights.
casey: uh
casey: not yet
cipher: Hm?
casey: the time lmao
cipher: Oh, right.
cipher: Well, try to get at least some sleep, we can talk more after school.
casey: ok

